<div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim</div>
<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Birchas HaMazon U'Mayim Acharonim<br><span style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:400;">Halachah 3 (§§ 1–16)</span></div>
<div class="lm-subtitle">Based on <span class="lr">LM I:34</span> (<span class="v">"V'Atem Tihyu Li Mamleches Kohanim"</span>)</div>

<!-- Intro -->
<div class="sn">Introduction: The Three <i>Nekudos</i> and the Broken Heart</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Disgrace has broken my heart"</span> (Tehillim 69) — disgraces and humiliations shatter a person's heart. The <span class="h">tikkun</span> is to connect one's heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> [holy point] relevant to one's heart at that time. The <span class="h">tzadik</span> rules — his essential dominion is to illuminate and awaken hearts for Hashem's service: <span class="v">"Yosef is the ruler."</span> This aspect of "Yosef the ruler" = <span class="h">mala fum</span> — the <span class="h">tzadik</span>'s mouth is full of Hashem's holiness. Therefore one must pray aloud, with the mouth, not thought alone.</div>

<div class="p">The essential framework: the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span> — the root of all Israel's souls. Initially, everyone must receive from the <span class="h">tzadik</span>. Afterward, each person receives from his fellow — for every Jew has a unique precious point that his fellow lacks, and regarding that point he is a "<span class="h">tzadik</span>" toward his fellow. One receives this by conversing with friends about <span class="h">yiras Shamayim</span>. Finally, each person receives from within himself (<span class="h">minei u'vei</span>) — illuminating his own <span class="h">nekudah</span> by speaking between himself and his Creator: <span class="v">"my mouth speaks wisdom"</span> — the <span class="h">nekudah</span> in the mouth illuminates the heart.</div>

<div class="p">Through these <span class="kc">three <span class="h">nekudos</span></span>, the disgraces besieging the heart are annulled. All evil desires come from the shattering of the vessels of <span class="h">Chesed</span> — from there all fallen loves, and from there all "disgraces of the heart." When one connects the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span>: <span class="v">"love covers all transgressions."</span> At the <span class="h">nekudah</span>, holy love dwells = <span class="h">Kohein</span>: <span class="v">"I give him My covenant of peace"</span> (said of Pinchas when he received the <span class="h">kehunah</span>). The <span class="h">Kohein</span> = holy love dwelling at the <span class="h">bris</span> = the <span class="h">tzadik</span> = the <span class="h">nekudah</span>. Through this, fallen loves are nullified.</div>

<!-- §1 -->
<div class="sn">§ 1 — Birchas HaMazon: Connecting the Heart to the <i>Nekudah</i></div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>. Everything a person eats and enjoys contains fallen loves that must be elevated and connected to holy love — <span class="v">"love in delights"</span>: all the world's pleasures must be raised to holy love. This is accomplished by connecting the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span>. All <span class="h">berachos</span> the Sages established — forbidding benefit without a <span class="h">berachah</span> — serve this purpose: through the <span class="h">berachah</span>, one connects the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span>, the source of all blessings: <span class="v">"blessings upon the head of the <span class="h">tzadik</span>."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> is the root from which the Sages derived all <span class="h">berachos</span>: <span class="mx">"if one blesses afterward, how much more so beforehand!"</span> The essential clarification of food occurs after eating — the good rises to the heart, the finest to the brain, the waste is expelled. <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> after eating ensures this clarification happens in holiness, connecting the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> in the mouth. Therefore <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> is specifically on bread: <span class="mx">"bread sustains the heart"</span> — the heart needs the most clarification from fallen loves. Three <span class="h">berachos</span> connect the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He ate and drank, and his heart was gladdened"</span> — this is <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>. Through it, the heart's evil (= fallen loves, broken heart) is annulled. The <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span> = good: <span class="v">"say of the <span class="h">tzadik</span>: he is good."</span> Therefore: <span class="kc">"his heart was gladdened"</span> through <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>.</div>

<!-- §2 -->
<div class="sn">§ 2 — Yosef the Ruler: Source of All Blessings and Satiation</div>

<div class="p">All sustenance and blessings flow from the <span class="h">tzadik</span> = <span class="v">"Yosef is the ruler over the land; he is the provider to all the people of the land."</span> Yosef = the seven years of plenty, subduing the seven years of famine = <span class="v">"disgrace of famine"</span> (<span class="h">cherpas ra'av</span>). Yosef sustains the entire world during famine: <span class="v">"G-d has gathered my disgrace"</span> — said of Yosef, who gathers and nullifies all disgrace.</div>

<div class="p">Pharaoh told the people: <span class="v">"Go to Yosef; whatever he tells you, do."</span> Rashi: they had stored grain but it rotted. Yosef told them to circumcise themselves. <span class="mx">"If he decreed on the grain and it rotted — what if he decrees on us and we die?"</span> — for Yosef = <span class="h">tzadik moshel</span> [the ruling <span class="h">tzadik</span>]; whoever distances from the <span class="h">nekudah</span> is far from blessing, and the years of famine overpower. All life comes only from the <span class="h">tzadik</span> = <span class="v">"the <span class="h">tzadik</span> — the life of all worlds."</span></div>

<div class="p">Even Yaakov and his sons — <span class="v">"Your people are all <span class="h">tzadikim</span>"</span> — could not receive sustenance except through Yosef, the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span>. Yaakov said: <span class="v">"go, buy us grain to break our hunger."</span> "<span class="h">Shever</span>" [grain/breaking] specifically — for the hunger comes from <span class="h">sheviras lev</span> [heartbreak] = <span class="v">"disgrace has broken my heart"</span> = <span class="h">cherpas ra'av</span>. The <span class="h">tikkun</span>: through Yosef, who brings satiation: <span class="v">"the <span class="h">tzadik</span> eats to satisfy his soul."</span></div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>: drawing blessing and satiation — <span class="v">"you shall eat, be satisfied, and bless."</span> The Zohar: <span class="mx">"Can one not be satisfied [without the blessing]? Rather, even if a person eats a little, and places the will of satiation upon it…"</span> — the essential satiation comes through <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> itself, connecting the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = Yosef the ruler, the provider. Through this, <span class="h">cherpas ra'av</span> is nullified, and blessing and satiation are sent into one's being.</div>

<!-- §3 -->
<div class="sn">§ 3 — Three <i>Berachos</i> = Three <i>Nekudos</i></div>

<div class="p">Three <span class="h">berachos</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> = three <span class="h">nekudos</span>: (1) the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span> of the <span class="h">tzadik</span> of the generation = Yosef; (2) the <span class="h">nekudah</span> one receives from one's fellow; (3) the <span class="h">nekudah</span> one receives from within oneself. All are aspects of <span class="h">tzadik</span>, where holy love = <span class="h">Kohein</span> dwells. Therefore one mentions <span class="h">bris</span>, Torah, life, and sustenance in <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — all aspects of the <span class="h">nekudah</span>/<span class="h">tzadik</span>. <span class="h">Bris</span> = Yosef. Torah = <span class="h">mala fum</span> = the <span class="h">nekudah</span>. Life and sustenance = from the <span class="h">tzadik</span> who is the source of life, nullifying <span class="h">sitra d'mosa</span> [the death-aspect].</div>

<!-- §4 -->
<div class="sn">§ 4 — <i>Zimun</i> with Three: Rebbe, Friends, Self</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Zimun</span> with three = three <span class="h">nekudos</span>. When three Jews sit at one table, all three <span class="h">nekudos</span> illuminate. The one who leads the <span class="h">zimun</span> (the greatest among them) is the <span class="h">nekudah</span> of the comprehensive <span class="h">tzadik</span> relative to the others. He illuminates them; they receive from him. Since they are two besides him, they also receive from each other (<span class="h">din min din</span>). And then each receives from within himself (<span class="h">minei u'vei</span>). Thus with three, all three <span class="h">nekudos</span> shine.</div>

<div class="p">Just as in learning: a Rebbe teaches two students. Afterward, the two review together — each illuminating the other, reminding what was forgotten, receiving <span class="h">din min din</span>. Then each reviews alone. So in <span class="h">avodas Hashem</span>: receive from the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, then from friends, then through personal <span class="h">hisbodedus</span>.</div>

<div class="p">An important person may not travel without two companions: <span class="v">"Avraham took his two lads."</span> The <span class="h">tzadik</span> always needs at least two to illuminate his <span class="h">nekudah</span> through all three levels. This is <span class="mx">"blessed is the Merciful One who gave a threefold Torah on the third day through a triple one"</span> — all Torah is "tripled" because it encompasses all three <span class="h">nekudos</span>. And the threefold priestly blessing = <span class="h">Kohein</span> = holy love at the <span class="h">nekudah</span>. With three at a table, the obligation to speak <span class="h">divrei Torah</span> is especially strong — for then the Torah's illumination is complete.</div>

<!-- §5 -->
<div class="sn">§ 5 — Perfection with Three</div>

<div class="p">The essential perfection of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> is with three, because wherever three Jews are, the greatest serves as the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span> relative to the two, and all three <span class="h">nekudos</span> shine.</div>

<!-- §6 -->
<div class="sn">§ 6 — <i>Zimun</i>: Preparing the Heart</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Zimun</span> = preparation. Every holy matter requires <span class="h">hachanah</span> [preparation] — preparing and inviting the heart to receive the <span class="h">nekudah</span>'s light: <span class="v">"prepare their hearts toward You."</span> <span class="mx">"Listen, my masters, we wish to bless"</span> — <span class="mx">"listening depends on the heart"</span>: incline your ears and hearts to the <span class="h">berachah</span>, connecting the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> in the mouth whence blessings emerge.</div>

<!-- §7 -->
<div class="sn">§ 7 — <i>HaTov V'HaMeitiv</i>: The <i>Nekudah</i> Is Good</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">HaTov V'HaMeitiv</span> was established at Yavneh for the dead of Beitar who were given burial. After receiving illumination from the three <span class="h">nekudos</span> through three <span class="h">berachos</span>, one blesses <span class="h">HaTov V'HaMeitiv</span>: the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span> = good: <span class="v">"say of the <span class="h">tzadik</span>: he is good."</span> "<span class="h">HaTov</span>" = good in itself; "<span class="h">V'HaMeitiv</span>" = does good to others — the <span class="h">nekudah</span> illuminates others, sending goodness to the heart, nullifying <span class="h">sheviras lev</span>: <span class="v">"he ate and drank, and his heart was gladdened"</span> = <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Burial = honor for the dead, covering shame. Through <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, the <span class="h">nekudah</span> shines, nullifying <span class="h">sitra d'mosa</span> [death-aspect from the shattering]. Burial conquers the death-aspect. All burial's power is through the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">bris</span>: Shem and Yefes covered their father's nakedness (= <span class="h">tikkun habris</span>) and merited burial.</div>

<!-- §8 -->
<div class="sn">§ 8 — The Cup: Ten Things, Wine, and Song</div>

<div class="p">The cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> requires ten things — for the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = the letter <span class="h">yud</span> (= 10) = holiness. The cup = <span class="h">Malchus</span>/mouth: <span class="v">"a cup of salvations I shall raise"</span> (Dovid). In the mouth = <span class="h">Malchus</span>, the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">mala fum</span> shines, connecting the heart upward.</div>

<div class="p">The wine of the cup of blessing: wine's <span class="h">tikkun</span> is through the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span> = <span class="h">tikkun habris</span>: <span class="mx">"whoever sees a <span class="h">sotah</span> in her disgrace should vow to abstain from wine."</span> Only through <span class="h">tikkun habris</span> can wine be drunk in holiness — then: <span class="v">"wine gladdens the heart of man."</span> Wine contains both aspects; the essential clarification occurs there. The root of all shattering was Adam's sin through the Tree of Knowledge = wine: <span class="mx">"she squeezed grapes and gave him."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"Song is said only over wine"</span> — all songs awaken and connect the heart to Hashem: <span class="v">"my heart and my flesh sing to the living G-d."</span> Song over wine = connecting the heart to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> in the mouth, rectifying the wine into <span class="v">"wine that gladdens."</span></div>

<!-- §9 -->
<div class="sn">§ 9 — <i>Chanukah</i>: Light of the <i>Nekudah</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span> = the light of the holy <span class="h">nekudah</span> that illuminates, awakens, and connects the heart to Hashem: <span class="v">"a <span class="h">mitzvah</span> is a lamp, and Torah is light."</span> The <span class="h">nekudah</span> = Torah = light = <span class="h">ner Chanukah</span>. The oil of <span class="h">ner Chanukah</span> = <span class="h">shemen mish'chas kodesh</span> = the holy <span class="h">mochin</span> [intellects] from which the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span> = Yosef the ruler is drawn: <span class="mx">"to draw holy anointing oil and kindle the lamp"</span> (Zohar) = drawing the <span class="h">nekudah</span> from the <span class="h">mochin</span>, and through it kindling the light that awakens the heart.</div>

<!-- §10 -->
<div class="sn">§ 10 — Kindling Each Year: Defeating <i>Malchus HaRish'ah</i></div>

<div class="p">We fulfill this <span class="h">mitzvah</span> each year to shatter the wicked kingdom that stands against us in every generation — <span class="v">"to make them forget Your Torah and transgress Your statutes."</span> The wicked kingdom's power comes from the shattering, from fallen loves = evil desires. They can only prevail when the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik moshel</span> = <span class="h">Malchus</span> of holiness does not shine. When it does shine, all shattering and disgrace are nullified and the wicked kingdom collapses.</div>

<div class="p">The Greeks wanted to abolish Torah entirely — to extinguish the <span class="h">nekudah</span>'s light. <span class="mx">"Write for yourselves on the horn of an ox that you have no share in the G-d of Israel"</span> — they wanted to nullify Israel's dominion, their status as <span class="v">"a portion of Hashem"</span>: <span class="v">"I am your portion and your inheritance."</span> Therefore they contaminated all the oils = the <span class="h">mochin</span> from which the <span class="h">nekudah</span> is drawn. The essential <span class="h">tzadik moshel</span> comes through guarding the <span class="h">mochin</span> = guarding the <span class="h">bris</span> = purifying the mind from impure thoughts. Yosef stood his test, did not blemish the <span class="h">mochin</span>, and merited <span class="v">"there is none as wise and discerning"</span> = <span class="v">"Yosef is the ruler."</span></div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">Chanukah</span> miracle was through <span class="h">Kohanim</span> = holy love dwelling at the <span class="h">bris shalom</span>, at the <span class="h">nekudah</span>. Through this, <span class="h">sheviras lev</span> is nullified, the wicked kingdom's sustenance cut, all desires and disgraces from fallen loves annulled.</div>

<!-- §11 -->
<div class="sn">§ 11 — The <i>Kohein Gadol</i>'s Oil and the <i>Even HaSh'siyah</i></div>

<div class="p">The true <span class="h">tzadik</span> of the generation is called <span class="h">Kohein</span>: <span class="v">"the lips of the <span class="h">Kohein</span> guard knowledge, and Torah is sought from his mouth."</span> The <span class="h">Chanukah</span> miracle came through oil sealed with the <span class="h">Kohein Gadol</span>'s seal = the <span class="h">tzadik</span> of the generation who guards the <span class="h">bris</span> completely. His <span class="h">mochin</span> = holy oil, sealed with the seal of holiness: <span class="v">"and his offspring He sealed."</span> Through his <span class="h">nekudah</span>, which draws from perfectly pure <span class="h">mochin</span>, the miracle occurred.</div>

<div class="p">In every generation, though the forces of evil contaminate all ordinary oils/<span class="h">mochin</span> — weakening every individual's <span class="h">nekudah</span> — Hashem sends a true <span class="h">tzadik</span> who guards the <span class="h">bris</span> completely, whose <span class="h">nekudah</span> has the power to illuminate all Israel. When each Jew receives from this comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span>, his own <span class="h">nekudah</span> is awakened, and through the holy love at the <span class="h">nekudah</span>, all <span class="h">sheviras lev</span> and the wicked kingdom are nullified.</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">Kohein Gadol</span> entered the <span class="h">Kodesh HaKodashim</span> with the <span class="h">ketores</span> [incense] upon the <span class="h">Even HaSh'siyah</span> [Foundation Stone] = the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span> = <span class="v">"the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is the foundation of the world."</span> Through the <span class="h">ketores</span> (= binding, from the root <span class="h">kesher</span> [knot]) he bound all fallen loves to the holy <span class="h">nekudah</span>: <span class="v">"love covers all transgressions."</span> <span class="v">"Oil and incense gladden the heart"</span> — the opposite of <span class="h">sheviras lev</span>. The <span class="h">ketores</span> was offered at the time of lighting the <span class="h">Menorah</span>: <span class="v">"when Aharon kindles the lamps… he shall burn the incense."</span></div>

<!-- §12 -->
<div class="sn">§ 12 — <i>Korbanos</i> of the <i>Nesi'im</i>: Inaugurating the Altar</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">korbanos</span> of the <span class="h">nesi'im</span> [tribal leaders] for the altar's inauguration, read on <span class="h">Chanukah</span>: every <span class="h">korban</span> was through the <span class="h">Kohein</span> who elevated the animal-loves (= fallen, beastly loves) to the holy <span class="h">nekudah</span>. The <span class="h">nesi'im</span> = the generation's <span class="h">tzadikim</span> = the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span>. Through their light, all ascend from profane to sacred. The altar and <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> = the heart: <span class="v">"My eyes and My heart shall be there."</span></div>

<!-- §13 -->
<div class="sn">§ 13 — <i>Chanukah</i> = Initiation into Service</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Chanukah</span> = <span class="h">chinuch</span> [initiation/training]. The essential training to enter Hashem's service is through the <span class="h">nekudah</span>: receiving from the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, then from friends, then from within oneself through <span class="h">hisbodedus</span>. Through this the <span class="h">nekudah</span> shines, connecting the heart to Hashem, nullifying all disgraces and desires. One ascends from profane to sacred. <span class="kc">The essential <span class="h">chinuch</span> to enter holiness is through <span class="h">hisbodedus</span></span> — personal prayer between oneself and one's Creator, which illuminates one's own <span class="h">nekudah</span>.</div>

<!-- §14 -->
<div class="sn">§ 14 — <i>Ner</i> = Three <i>Yichudim</i></div>

<div class="p">The kavanos teach that <span class="h">ner</span> [lamp] = in <span class="h">gematriyah</span>, three <span class="h">yichudim</span> [unifications] = three <span class="h">nekudos</span>. Each <span class="h">nekudah</span> = <span class="h">tzadik</span>, through whom the essential <span class="h">yichud</span> occurs. By receiving from all three <span class="h">nekudos</span>, the heart is illuminated and awakened = <span class="h">ner Chanukah</span>.</div>

<!-- §15 -->
<div class="sn">§ 15 — <i>Ish U'Veiso</i>, <i>Mehadrin</i>, <i>Mehadrin Min HaMehadrin</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"<span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span>: a person and his household. The <span class="h">mehadrin</span>: a lamp for each person. The <span class="h">mehadrin min ha'mehadrin</span>: adding each day."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="kc"><span class="h">Ish u'veiso</span></span> = the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span>: the head of the household is the ruler, encompassing all, the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span> relative to his family. Just as in <span class="h">klal</span> [the general picture], the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span> of all Israel — so in <span class="h">prat</span> [the particular], there are leaders of thousands, of hundreds, and every householder who leads his family. Each is a comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span> relative to those beneath him — like a tree with branches and sub-branches (as in <span class="lr">LM I:69</span>). When <span class="h">ish u'veiso</span> kindles, all other <span class="h">nekudos</span> are automatically illuminated.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="kc"><span class="h">Mehadrin</span></span> — a lamp for each person = the illumination of each individual's <span class="h">nekudah</span>, which can illuminate and awaken another's heart.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="kc"><span class="h">Mehadrin min ha'mehadrin</span></span> — adding each day = the <span class="h">nekudah</span> of each person shining from within himself (<span class="h">minei u'vei</span>), its light increasing daily through constant awakening, until the <span class="kc">eighth day</span> = the completion of the <span class="h">nekudah</span>'s light = <span class="h">tzadik</span> = <span class="h">milah</span> (given on the eighth day) = <span class="h">bris</span>.</div>

<!-- §16 -->
<div class="sn">§ 16 — From Nightfall Until the Foot Ceases from the Market</div>

<div class="p"><span class="mx">"<span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span>: from when the stars emerge until the foot ceases from the marketplace."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Stars"</span> = <span class="v">"those who bring the many to righteousness, like the stars"</span> = the <span class="h">nekudos</span>, which are called <span class="h">matzdikei harabim</span> [those who make the many righteous]: through them, people enter holiness. They are <span class="h">tzadik</span> = stars of light: <span class="v">"light is sown for the <span class="h">tzadik</span>."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Until the foot ceases from the marketplace"</span> — when the heart is sunk in disgraces/desires = <span class="v">"her feet descend…"</span> Through the <span class="h">nekudah</span>'s light, <span class="h">sheviras lev</span> (<span class="h">sitra d'mosa</span>) is nullified, the feet of holiness rise from the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> = the foot ceases from the marketplace (= the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>'s domain).</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Chanukah</span> days are days of prayer and thanksgiving: <span class="mx">"they established eight days of <span class="h">Chanukah</span> to give thanks and praise."</span> The essence of prayer and thanksgiving = the light of the <span class="h">nekudah</span>: <span class="v">"my mouth speaks wisdom"</span> shining into the heart. We read <span class="h">Parshas Mikeitz</span> on <span class="h">Chanukah</span> — for it speaks of Yosef achieving rulership = <span class="v">"Yosef is the ruler"</span> = the comprehensive <span class="h">nekudah</span>.</div>

<div class="sep">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

<div class="sn">Addendum (linked to Birchas HaMazon above)</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"They drank and became intoxicated with him"</span> (Bereishis 43). The Sages: <span class="mx">"from the day Yosef parted from his brothers, they did not drink wine."</span> Wine cannot be drunk in holiness except when all Israel gather together with Yosef the <span class="h">tzadik</span>. When the <span class="h">nekudah</span> shines in all Israel, <span class="h">cherpas lev</span> is nullified, and wine = <span class="v">"wine gladdens the heart."</span> This = the cup of wine of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> with three. <span class="v">"With him"</span> specifically — through drawing near to the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = Yosef.</div>

<div class="p">The custom of fragrant oil before <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>: <span class="mx">"sanctify yourselves, be holy"</span> = fragrant oil. Oil = the <span class="h">nekudah</span>'s light = <span class="h">shemen mish'chas kodesh</span> = <span class="h">ner Chanukah</span>'s oil. Applied before <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> so the <span class="h">nekudah</span> shines fully during the blessing.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Tzedakah</span> given on <span class="h">Chanukah</span> = <span class="v">"the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is gracious and gives"</span>: holy love = <span class="h">chesed</span> = Avraham dwells at the <span class="h">nekudah</span> = Yosef the <span class="h">tzadik</span>. Therefore: <span class="v">"the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is gracious and gives"</span> = <span class="v">"Yosef sustained his father and brothers."</span> On <span class="h">Chanukah</span>, when drawing the <span class="h">nekudah</span>'s light through <span class="h">ner Chanukah</span>, we increase <span class="h">tzedakah</span>.</div>

<div class="ts">
  <div class="sh">✦ Translator's Summary — Halachah 3 ✦</div>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>Core concept</strong>: <em>"Disgrace has broken my heart"</em> — all evil desires come from shattered vessels of <em>Chesed</em> (= fallen loves). The <em>tikkun</em>: connect the heart to the <em>nekudah</em> [holy point] = the <em>tzadik</em>. Three <em>nekudos</em>: (1) the comprehensive <em>tzadik</em> of the generation; (2) the unique point in one's fellow; (3) one's own inner point, accessed through <em>hisbodedus</em>.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§1-2</strong>: <em>Birchas HaMazon</em> connects the heart to the <em>nekudah</em> in the mouth. Everything eaten contains fallen loves that must be elevated. Bread sustains the heart → needs the most clarification. Yosef = source of all sustenance = nullifies <em>cherpas ra'av</em>. Satiation itself comes through <em>Birchas HaMazon</em>.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§3-6</strong>: Three <em>berachos</em> = three <em>nekudos</em>. <em>Zimun</em> with three actualizes all three levels. Like a Rebbe with two students: learn from the teacher, review with each other, then study alone. <em>Zimun</em> = preparing the heart.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§7-8</strong>: <em>HaTov V'HaMeitiv</em> for burial at Beitar — burial covers shame, the <em>nekudah</em> nullifies the death-aspect. The cup requires ten things (= <em>yud</em> = <em>nekudah</em>). Wine = the heart's <em>tikkun</em> through <em>tikkun habris</em>. "Song only over wine" = connecting the heart to the <em>nekudah</em>.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§9-11</strong>: <em>Ner Chanukah</em> = the <em>nekudah</em>'s light. The Greeks contaminated all oils/<em>mochin</em>; the miracle was through the <em>Kohein Gadol</em>'s sealed oil = the <em>tzadik</em> of the generation. The <em>Kohein Gadol</em> entered the <em>Kodesh HaKodashim</em> with <em>ketores</em> upon the <em>Even HaSh'siyah</em> = the <em>nekudah</em> = <em>tzadik yesod olam</em>.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§12-16</strong>: <em>Nesi'im</em>'s <em>korbanos</em> = inaugurating the altar through the comprehensive <em>nekudah</em>. <em>Chanukah</em> = initiation through <em>hisbodedus</em>. Three levels of <em>ner Chanukah</em> (<em>ish u'veiso</em>, <em>mehadrin</em>, <em>mehadrin min ha'mehadrin</em>) = three <em>nekudos</em>. "Stars" = <em>matzdikei harabim</em>. "Foot ceases from marketplace" = fallen desires nullified.</p>
</div>

